 "caveats": "Segments are hand-assigned from route order and HM/item gates (Old Rod after Dewford, Good Rod on Route 118 before gym 3, Rock Smash after badge 3, Go-Goggles for the desert after badge 4, Surf after badge 5, Devon Scope and Super Rod after badge 6, Dive after badge 7, Waterfall after badge 8). Locations that open partway are graded by their main encounter area, so a few mons on mixed routes (Route 118 west vs east, Route 115, Route 123) may be a segment early or late. Regis are placed before the Elite Four because the Sealed Chamber puzzle only needs Dive, Relicanth and Wailord, though most players do it after. Latios/Latias count as the post-game roamer (Southern Island needs the event-only Eon Ticket); Sky Pillar, Rayquaza and Beldum are post-game; event-only Jirachi, Celebi, Mew and Deoxys are excluded."
